                <pb facs="0606" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg486"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Steering Committee/200: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France (Marriner) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-11-29T19:00:00+00:00">November 29,
                            1932—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 29—5:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>679. From Norman Davis. I have just
                    learned that Mr. MacDonald and Sir John Simon are leaving Thursday<anchor
                        n="97" xml:id="d330-f1"/> and expect to arrive in Geneva on Friday morning.
                    Previous to this Simon had informed me in
                    writing that the Prime Minister had told him that when he went to Geneva he
                    would like an opportunity to discuss with the representatives of the other
                    principal powers the situation in regard to the proposed world economic
                    conference and Simon has so informed
                        von Neurath, Paul-Boncour, and Aloisi. He stated that he <pb facs="0607" n="487" xml:id="pg487"
                    /> was doing this “so that we may be all prepared for some discussion on the
                    subject”.</p>
                <p>I plan to return to Geneva tomorrow, Wednesday, night. [Davis.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marriner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
